Pe dată de 2011-06-20 08:32, Viddaric a scris:
> In vanilla Nethack, what is, in your opinion, the hardest class to
> ascend as, and which is the easiest?
> 
> One would be tempted to say Tourist for hardest, but they actually
> have a lot of advantages. They can get Skilled in silver sabers, so
> they're great melee combatants once they get Grayswandir (Strength is
> easy to train anyway) and of course they get infinite blessed
> charging, MR, telepathy, and half spell damage with the PYEC. It's
> also tempting to say Knight, because of their stubpar (for a fighter)
> starting stats and the whole code of conduct crap, but they can get
> Expert in riding and several powerful weapon skills, so as long as
> they keep a saddled pet, they also have a good chance. Personally, I'd
> go with Monks. Natural intrinsic skills and powerful martial arts
> can't make up for a -20 hit penalty for wearing DSM and the complete
> inability to proficiently wield any artifact weapon other than the
> SoA. Not to mention the vegetarian conduct and lack of a good ranged
> weapon for once their Power runs out.
> 
> As for easiest, I'm not sure... I have yet to make my YAFAP, although
> the character I've gotten closest with is still alive. He's an Elven
> Ranger, but the only reason it's so easy for him is because I was
> lucky enough to find a +5 scale mail on dlvl 1, which, in AC terms, is
> as good as +0 DSM. After acquiring reflection from no less than three
> different sources (sokoban amulet, SoR, LoD) it's been pretty much
> smooth sailing, although I have yet to find MR, which worries me.
> Anyway, It seems like rangers do have a pretty easy early game, due to
> their powerful ranged attacks. 4 arrows in a turn is nothing to scoff
> at, and intrinsic stealth and searching don't hurt either. Are rangers
> one of the easier classes to play, or am I going to get hosed in the
> late game? What do you think is the easiest class to ascend as?
Since the only class I've yet ascended is wizard, I'd be tempted to say
it's the easiest (at least, once you get past the early game).  I'm now
trying some tourists, which I find considerably harder.  I also have
some experience with priests, a role which makes pressing your luck
early much easier with their automatic B/C/U identification.  Had some
monks as well, I'd rate them somewhere between priest and tourist.
Don't have much experience with fighter-style classes, yet.

Benjamin


